00:00:02,265 --> 00:00:07,565
Ho ,oba, Ho ,obi,

2
00:00:07,925 --> 00:00:11,685
Mama, Ho ,obi, Siune!

3
00:00:12,285 --> 00:00:18,345
Ho ,aji, Seal, Zimbabu, S gegangen,
vos, ent ententes get ridin' Hi there!

4
00:00:18,465 --> 00:00:19,982
Time for this week's M .M .O .S.

5
00:00:20,065 --> 00:00:20,895
stream.

6
00:00:20,978 --> 00:00:22,722
You just saw a promo of
today's featured game.

7
00:00:22,805 --> 00:00:25,322
And this is what last week's
launch day looked like!

8
00:00:25,405 --> 00:00:27,702
Can you guess what everyone's
waiting in line for?

9
00:00:27,785 --> 00:00:29,065
Sword Art Online!

10
00:00:29,665 --> 00:00:33,162
The first person in line said
they camped out for three days.

11
00:00:33,245 --> 00:00:36,539
Hey, but if you're a hardcore
gamer, that's what you do.

12
00:00:36,965 --> 00:00:39,141
On today's episode of the MMO Stream,

13
00:00:39,245 --> 00:00:42,962
we'll be covering the internationally
famous Sword Art Online, a .k .a.

14
00:00:43,045 --> 00:00:44,545
FAO. Up to now,

15
00:00:44,705 --> 00:00:46,622
none of the Nerf Gear
software we've seen has taken

16
00:00:46,705 --> 00:00:49,302
advantage of the
possibilities of the hardware.

17
00:00:49,385 --> 00:00:51,145
Hey, I'm off to practice now.

18
00:00:51,825 --> 00:00:52,742
See you later, okay?

19
00:00:52,825 --> 00:00:55,605
by the inventor of their
gear, Akihiko Gabe.

20
00:00:55,885 --> 00:01:00,445
Heck, this is the VR MMORPG that me and
everyone else have been waiting for.

21
00:01:00,685 --> 00:01:02,861
The beta testers say it's incredible.

22
00:01:02,965 --> 00:01:04,502
I wish I could have gotten one.

23
00:01:04,585 --> 00:01:07,725
The first testing was limited
to only 10,000 copies.

24
00:01:08,125 --> 00:01:12,596
Those fans in line snapped them up, and
online the game sold out in seconds.

25
00:01:27,005 --> 00:01:28,445
Link, start!

26
00:02:00,825 --> 00:02:02,165
Hello, world.

27
00:02:02,605 --> 00:02:03,805
I'm back.

28
00:02:32,465 --> 00:02:34,502
Well, I told him, so it's his deal.

29
00:02:34,585 --> 00:02:35,842
Why don't we form a party?

30
00:02:35,925 --> 00:02:39,725
Well, I don't know, maybe.
Oh, come on. It'll be great.

31
00:02:40,505 --> 00:02:42,623
We can go out and do that bad stuff.

32
00:02:44,765 --> 00:02:46,845
Hey, Froze! Wait up!

33
00:02:49,865 --> 00:02:50,695
What's up?

34
00:02:51,125 --> 00:02:51,955
Woo!

35
00:02:54,145 --> 00:02:56,102
You act like you know
your way around here.

36
00:02:56,185 --> 00:02:58,422
You were in the beta test, weren't you?

37
00:02:58,505 --> 00:02:59,335
Yeah.

38
00:02:59,525 --> 00:03:00,355
Cool.

39
00:03:00,438 --> 00:03:01,620
Today's my first day.

40
00:03:01,825 --> 00:03:04,462
So, could you give me some
tips on the lower floors?

41
00:03:04,545 --> 00:03:05,762
Yeah, I don't know if...

42
00:03:05,845 --> 00:03:07,865
Aw, please, I'm begging you.

43
00:03:08,365 --> 00:03:09,659
Look, my name's Klein.

44
00:03:09,965 --> 00:03:10,965
Good to meet you.

45
00:03:12,385 --> 00:03:14,045
Alright, I'm Kirito.

46
00:03:18,545 --> 00:03:20,445
Right in the nuts.

47
00:03:21,125 --> 00:03:21,955
Kill me now.

48
00:03:22,038 --> 00:03:23,278
Oh, come on, seriously.

49
00:03:23,465 --> 00:03:25,025
You can't feel any pain.

50
00:03:26,545 --> 00:03:27,622
Oh, yeah, you're right.

51
00:03:27,705 --> 00:03:28,765
Sorry, habit.

52
00:03:29,185 --> 00:03:30,420
Remember what I said?

53
00:03:30,525 --> 00:03:32,701
The first move is the most important.

54
00:03:32,885 --> 00:03:34,822
Yeah, that's easy for you to say.

55
00:03:34,905 --> 00:03:36,705
But he won't stand still.

56
00:03:38,185 --> 00:03:40,325
If you do your initial motion right

57
00:03:41,325 --> 00:03:44,025
and activate a sword
skill at the right time,

58
00:03:50,305 --> 00:03:54,062
The system pretty much guarantees
you'll always hit your target.

59
00:03:54,145 --> 00:03:55,405
Initial motion?

60
00:03:57,285 --> 00:03:59,344
Here's an easier way to look at it.

61
00:04:01,485 --> 00:04:04,242
Right after you start your
move, wait for a little bit.

62
00:04:04,325 --> 00:04:07,737
When you feel the skills start
to activate, drive it home.

63
00:04:07,945 --> 00:04:09,025
Drive it home?

64
00:04:14,065 --> 00:04:15,465
Woo!

65
00:04:20,485 --> 00:04:21,885
Yaaah!

66
00:04:32,985 --> 00:04:35,025
Yaaah! Yaaah!

67
00:04:35,845 --> 00:04:36,825
Congratulations.

68
00:04:39,025 --> 00:04:41,105
That was nice.

69
00:04:42,525 --> 00:04:45,682
But that boar's about as weak
as slimes in other games are.

70
00:04:45,765 --> 00:04:47,422
Holy crap, you gotta be kidding.

71
00:04:47,505 --> 00:04:49,976
I thought that thing was a mid-level boss.

72
00:04:50,225 --> 00:04:51,545
Yeah, as if.

73
00:04:54,105 --> 00:04:54,935
Whoa!

74
00:04:55,705 --> 00:04:56,682
Addictive, isn't it?

75
00:04:56,765 --> 00:04:57,595
I'll say.

76
00:04:59,885 --> 00:05:05,025
So these skills, there's a ton of them,
like blacksmithing and stuff, right? Uh-huh.

77
00:05:06,045 --> 00:05:08,927
I heard the game has an
unlimited number of them.

78
00:05:09,145 --> 00:05:10,851
All except for magic, though.

79
00:05:12,565 --> 00:05:14,525
An RPG without magic?

80
00:05:14,765 --> 00:05:16,465
That's a bold decision, man!

81
00:05:21,225 --> 00:05:22,519
So, what do you think?

82
00:05:22,625 --> 00:05:25,722
It's kind of fun to move your
body as you fight, isn't it?

83
00:05:25,805 --> 00:05:27,005
Oh, hells yeah!

84
00:05:29,025 --> 00:05:30,385
You ready to move on?

85
00:05:31,125 --> 00:05:31,955
Yeah, man!

86
00:05:32,225 --> 00:05:33,225
Let's keep going!

87
00:05:41,605 --> 00:05:45,342
When I look around I can't
believe it we're inside

88
00:05:45,425 --> 00:05:51,522
a game bro whoever made
it's a genius this thing's

89
00:05:51,605 --> 00:05:55,242
amazing makes me glad I
was born when I was you

90
00:05:55,325 --> 00:05:58,762
know it's not that big
a deal cut me some slack

91
00:05:58,845 --> 00:06:01,482
it's my first full dive
you never used the nerve

92
00:06:01,565 --> 00:06:04,262
gear before today huh
this is your first time

93
00:06:04,345 --> 00:06:07,502
ever uh-huh as soon as
I got the money together

94
00:06:07,585 --> 00:06:10,644
I rushed out and bought all
the hardware to play SAO

95
00:06:10,805 --> 00:06:13,742
Stood in line and scored one
of the 10,000 hard copies.

96
00:06:13,825 --> 00:06:16,119
Guess you could say I was pretty lucky.

97
00:06:16,365 --> 00:06:20,365
Although, you, sir, were ten times
as lucky getting the beta tested.

98
00:06:20,885 --> 00:06:23,473
Dude, only a thousand
people got the chance.

99
00:06:23,925 --> 00:06:25,625
Yeah, I guess I was lucky.

100
00:06:26,645 --> 00:06:29,410
Hey, mind if I ask how
far you got in the beta?

101
00:06:29,845 --> 00:06:32,845
Two months and I couldn't
get further than Floor 8.

102
00:06:33,045 --> 00:06:35,542
But now I think I can
get there within a month.

103
00:06:35,625 --> 00:06:36,455
Easy.

104
00:06:37,205 --> 00:06:39,142
Sounds to me like you're really into this.

105
00:06:39,225 --> 00:06:41,025
Yeah, you could say that.

106
00:06:41,365 --> 00:06:45,725
During the beta test, SAO was the
only thing on my mind, day and night.

107
00:06:47,005 --> 00:06:51,025
In this world, a single blade can
take you anywhere you want to go.

108
00:06:51,625 --> 00:06:53,801
And even though it's a virtual world,

109
00:06:54,025 --> 00:06:57,665
I feel more alive in here than
I ever did in the real one.

110
00:07:01,645 --> 00:07:03,602
Anyway, you want to go
do some more hunting?

111
00:07:03,685 --> 00:07:04,825
But you know it.

112
00:07:05,285 --> 00:07:09,445
But the thing is, I'm really hungry.

113
00:07:09,785 --> 00:07:11,045
I have to log out.

114
00:07:11,205 --> 00:07:14,702
Too bad the food you eat here only
satisfies your hunger virtually.

115
00:07:14,785 --> 00:07:15,822
Yeah, for reals.

116
00:07:15,905 --> 00:07:18,165
That's why I ordered a pizza for 5.30.

117
00:07:18,345 --> 00:07:19,757
Wow, you're so prepared.

118
00:07:20,705 --> 00:07:21,535
You know it.

119
00:07:21,618 --> 00:07:24,222
Besides, the game can wait
until I get my pizza on.

120
00:07:24,305 --> 00:07:25,145
I guess.

121
00:07:26,445 --> 00:07:29,702
Hey, I was going to go meet up with
some people I know from another game.

122
00:07:29,785 --> 00:07:32,903
I don't know what you're up
to after this, so if, uh,

123
00:07:33,025 --> 00:07:36,496
you know, if you want, you can
friend him and hang with us.

124
00:07:37,985 --> 00:07:40,045
No, it's cool if you don't want to.

125
00:07:40,145 --> 00:07:40,975
No pressure.

126
00:07:41,058 --> 00:07:44,002
I can always introduce you to
him another time or something.

127
00:07:44,085 --> 00:07:45,045
Yeah, sorry.

128
00:07:46,285 --> 00:07:47,115
Thanks anyway.

129
00:07:47,645 --> 00:07:48,475
No way.

130
00:07:48,558 --> 00:07:50,422
I should be doing all the thanking.

131
00:07:50,505 --> 00:07:53,762
Hey, one of these days, I promise
I'll pay you back for all your help.

132
00:07:53,845 --> 00:07:54,963
Virtually, that is.

133
00:07:55,805 --> 00:07:56,635
Yeah, right.

134
00:07:56,845 --> 00:07:58,142
Thanks for everything, man.

135
00:07:58,225 --> 00:07:59,055
Really.

136
00:07:59,785 --> 00:08:01,482
Guess I'll see you around then.

137
00:08:01,565 --> 00:08:04,741
If there's anything else you
want to know, message me.

138
00:08:05,125 --> 00:08:05,955
Sweet!

139
00:08:06,105 --> 00:08:07,145
I'll do that.

140
00:08:14,125 --> 00:08:14,955
Huh?

141
00:08:16,405 --> 00:08:18,125
Where'd the logout button go?

142
00:08:18,505 --> 00:08:19,645
It should be there.

143
00:08:21,325 --> 00:08:22,885
Nope, it's not there.

144
00:08:23,845 --> 00:08:26,433
It should be at the
bottom of the main menu.

145
00:08:30,365 --> 00:08:31,425
See, not there.

146
00:08:31,745 --> 00:08:33,185
You're right, it's not.

147
00:08:34,265 --> 00:08:36,902
Oh well, today's what,
the first day out of beta?

148
00:08:36,985 --> 00:08:38,502
There's bound to be some bugs.

149
00:08:38,585 --> 00:08:41,585
I bet the server people
are freaking out right now.

150
00:08:42,305 --> 00:08:43,825
You will too. Huh?

151
00:08:44,145 --> 00:08:45,685
Look, it's 525.

152
00:08:47,865 --> 00:08:50,962
Oh my god, my teriyaki
mayo pizza and gingerbread!

153
00:08:51,045 --> 00:08:53,574
Why don't you just
contact the Game Master?

154
00:08:54,565 --> 00:08:56,742
Yeah, I did that, but nothing's happening.

155
00:08:56,825 --> 00:08:57,655
He's not picking up.

156
00:08:57,738 --> 00:09:01,074
Do you know if there's another
way to log out of this thing?

157
00:09:04,565 --> 00:09:07,545
No, whenever a player
wants to log out of SAO,

158
00:09:07,725 --> 00:09:10,222
the only way they can do it
is by going through the menu.

159
00:09:10,305 --> 00:09:11,462
That can't be right.

160
00:09:11,545 --> 00:09:13,602
There's got to be some other way out.

161
00:09:13,685 --> 00:09:16,005
Return! Log out! Escape!

162
00:09:22,885 --> 00:09:23,802
Told you so.

163
00:09:23,885 --> 00:09:27,120
And there was no emergency
logout in the manual either.

164
00:09:27,745 --> 00:09:30,725
No way. You're kidding. I know.

165
00:09:30,945 --> 00:09:34,265
I'll just rip the nerve gear
off my head. Don't bother.

166
00:09:34,645 --> 00:09:38,362
Once you're hooked in, you can't move
your body in the real world anymore.

167
00:09:38,445 --> 00:09:41,182
The nerve gear intercepts all
the commands you give from

168
00:09:41,265 --> 00:09:44,441
inside the game using an
interface built into the rig.

169
00:09:46,485 --> 00:09:47,315
Seriously?

170
00:09:47,398 --> 00:09:50,342
So now we gotta wait until someone
gets around to fixing the bug?

171
00:09:50,425 --> 00:09:51,255
That.

172
00:09:51,338 --> 00:09:55,402
Or until someone in the real world comes
along and takes the nerve gear off us.

173
00:09:55,485 --> 00:09:56,315
That's it.

174
00:09:57,685 --> 00:09:59,205
I live alone. You?

175
00:10:00,345 --> 00:10:02,005
I got a mom and a sister,

176
00:10:02,265 --> 00:10:05,782
and I'm pretty sure they'll notice
by dinnertime and come look at me.

177
00:10:05,865 --> 00:10:07,842
You got a sister? How old's she?

178
00:10:07,925 --> 00:10:08,866
What's she like?

179
00:10:09,645 --> 00:10:13,262
She's into sports and hates games,
and she's totally not your type, man.

180
00:10:13,345 --> 00:10:15,082
She wouldn't date a gamer
if he's the last guy.

181
00:10:15,165 --> 00:10:15,995
Who cares?

182
00:10:16,078 --> 00:10:16,908
I want to go!

183
00:10:19,085 --> 00:10:21,462
All right, getting kicked
in the balls doesn't hurt.

184
00:10:21,545 --> 00:10:22,375
Get serious.

185
00:10:22,545 --> 00:10:24,310
Don't you think this is weird?

186
00:10:24,485 --> 00:10:25,365
Yeah, totally.

187
00:10:25,725 --> 00:10:26,985
But it's just a bug.

188
00:10:27,485 --> 00:10:28,779
This isn't just a bug.

189
00:10:29,365 --> 00:10:33,836
If we can't log out, it's going to cause
some serious problems for the game.

190
00:10:35,125 --> 00:10:36,865
Yeah, I guess you're right.

191
00:10:37,605 --> 00:10:40,562
I wonder if the developers
even know what's happening.

192
00:10:40,645 --> 00:10:43,562
Because they could just shut down
the server and log everyone out.

193
00:10:43,645 --> 00:10:46,116
But why haven't they made an announcement?

194
00:11:16,045 --> 00:11:17,885
Do you know what's going on?

195
00:11:18,925 --> 00:11:20,925
Uh-uh, someone forced to teleport.

196
00:11:25,105 --> 00:11:27,205
What's going on with you? Huh?

197
00:11:28,925 --> 00:11:30,465
Look, up there.

198
00:11:35,005 --> 00:11:36,085
Now what?

199
00:11:52,925 --> 00:11:54,985
What the hell is that thing?

200
00:12:01,185 --> 00:12:02,845
Is that the game master?

201
00:12:02,965 --> 00:12:04,042
Why doesn't he have a face?

202
00:12:04,125 --> 00:12:04,955
Is this an event?

203
00:12:05,038 --> 00:12:07,185
I'm scared. Don't worry.

204
00:12:07,445 --> 00:12:09,739
It's just part of the opening ceremony.

205
00:12:10,585 --> 00:12:11,805
Attention, players.

206
00:12:12,305 --> 00:12:15,285
I welcome you to my world.

207
00:12:15,645 --> 00:12:16,998
What's he mean by that?

208
00:12:17,225 --> 00:12:23,585
My name is Akihiko Kayaba, and as of this
moment, I am in control of this world.

209
00:12:25,945 --> 00:12:26,775
Seriously?

210
00:12:26,858 --> 00:12:27,763
Is that really you?

211
00:12:27,945 --> 00:12:33,382
I'm sure most of you have already noticed
an item missing from your main menus.

212
00:12:33,465 --> 00:12:35,105
the logout button.

213
00:12:36,005 --> 00:12:39,305
Let me assure you, this is
not a defect in the game.

214
00:12:39,885 --> 00:12:42,445
I repeat, this is not a defect.

215
00:12:42,905 --> 00:12:46,085
This is how Sword Art
Online was designed to be.

216
00:12:46,485 --> 00:12:47,925
He's kidding, right?

217
00:12:48,305 --> 00:12:51,085
You cannot log yourselves out of SAO?

218
00:12:51,905 --> 00:12:54,442
and no one from the outside
will be able to shut down.

219
00:12:54,525 --> 00:12:56,878
or remove the nerve gear from your head.

220
00:12:57,485 --> 00:12:59,585
If anyone attempts to do so,

221
00:12:59,845 --> 00:13:03,282
a transmitter inside the nerve gear
will discharge a microwave signal?

222
00:13:03,365 --> 00:13:07,505
into your skull, destroying your
brain, and ending your life.

223
00:13:07,805 --> 00:13:09,142
What are you talking about?

224
00:13:09,225 --> 00:13:10,637
Come on, that's such BS.

225
00:13:11,005 --> 00:13:12,299
Let's get out of here.

226
00:13:14,125 --> 00:13:15,985
Hey, I can't get out.

227
00:13:16,945 --> 00:13:18,769
Are you listening to this crap?

228
00:13:19,085 --> 00:13:20,673
He's got to be nuts, right?

229
00:13:20,945 --> 00:13:23,145
Right, Kirito? He's not.

230
00:13:23,425 --> 00:13:26,862
The transmitter signals in the
headgear work just like microwaves.

231
00:13:26,945 --> 00:13:29,562
If the safety's disabled,
it could fry your brain.

232
00:13:29,645 --> 00:13:31,882
Couldn't someone cut the power, or...

233
00:13:31,965 --> 00:13:32,795
That won't work.

234
00:13:32,878 --> 00:13:35,138
The Nervegear's got an internal battery.

235
00:13:37,965 --> 00:13:39,365
This is crazy.

236
00:13:39,625 --> 00:13:40,743
It's totally crazy.

237
00:13:41,065 --> 00:13:42,285
Despite my warning,

238
00:13:42,765 --> 00:13:44,222
the families and friends of some of the

239
00:13:44,305 --> 00:13:46,642
players have attempted
removing the Nervegear.

240
00:13:46,725 --> 00:13:49,196
An unfortunate decision, to say the least.

241
00:13:49,825 --> 00:13:55,125
As a result, the game now has 213
less players than when it began.

242
00:13:55,625 --> 00:13:59,245
They've been deleted from both
Aincrad and the real world.

243
00:14:00,565 --> 00:14:01,395
213?

244
00:14:01,478 --> 00:14:02,308
No way.

245
00:14:02,785 --> 00:14:03,882
I don't believe it!

246
00:14:03,965 --> 00:14:05,125
As you can see,

247
00:14:05,445 --> 00:14:09,222
international media outlets have
round-the-clock coverage of everything,

248
00:14:09,305 --> 00:14:10,540
including the deaths.

249
00:14:11,185 --> 00:14:12,365
At this point,

250
00:14:12,565 --> 00:14:17,447
it's safe to assume the likelihood of a
Nervegear being removed is minimal at best.

251
00:14:17,905 --> 00:14:21,964
I hope this brings you a little
comfort as you try to clear the game.

252
00:14:24,105 --> 00:14:26,576
It's important you remember the following.

253
00:14:26,785 --> 00:14:30,362
There is no longer any way to
revive someone within the game.

254
00:14:30,445 --> 00:14:36,625
If your HP drops to zero, your avatar
will be deleted from the system forever,

255
